{
 "note": "Static diagnostic: do bubbles of different sizes restore the cohesion of a compact cluster?\n\nusage (from the repository): PYTHONPATH=. python poly_static.py CHI_GRID.json OUT.json\nClusters: monolayers (z = 0) packed around a centre with a 0.7 um surface gap (as AG32_local,\nmean gap 0.71 um), radii monodisperse 1.78 um or lognormal with median 1.78 um and geometric\nstandard deviation s (clipped to 0.5-5.5 um, SonoVue diameters 1-11 um); also AG32_local itself.\nResponse: linear APECSS chi(R) (CHI_GRID.json, same shell parameters for every size).\nField: direct FNM at the bubbles, 1000 Pa-eq (linear regime): one X+ disc alone and the X pair.\nModels: \"isolated\" (each bubble responds to the incident field only, like the pairwise model\nwithout its two-bubble feedback) and \"collective\" (u = (I + chi K)^-1 chi P with the\npropagation delay). Forces with the bare monopole formulas (no soft core) for every case:\nF1_i = -1/2 Re[V_i conj(grad P_i)], pair force on i from j\n-rho w^2 / (8 pi d^2) Re[V_i conj(V_j) e^{ikd}(1 - ikd)] r_hat(j->i).\nReported per cluster: median |u_i| / |chi_i P_i|; neighbour attraction (pairs with surface gap\n< 1 um): median of the attractive component and fraction repulsive; spread of F1 about its\nmean (rms); cohesion ratio = median neighbour attraction / rms F1 spread.\n",
